Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the project

✅ Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

## Changes Made:

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json with the new dependency

### 2. Code Implementation
- Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` to add Vercel Web Analytics
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the body element of the root layout

## Framework-Specific Details:
This project uses Next.js 16.3.6 with the App Router, so the implementation followed the Next.js App Router instructions:
- The Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`)
- The component is placed at the end of the body element, after the {children} prop
- This ensures analytics tracking is available across all pages of the application

## Verification Steps Completed:
✅ Build test passed - `npm run build` completed successfully
✅ Linting passed - `npm run lint` completed with no errors
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ All 14 routes generated successfully

## Files Modified:
- package.json - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- package-lock.json - Updated with new package and dependencies
- src/app/layout.tsx - Added Analytics import and component

## Next Steps for Deployment:
To enable Web Analytics in production:
1. Navigate to your Vercel project dashboard
2. Go to the Analytics section
3. Click the "Enable" button to activate analytics
4. Deploy this code to Vercel
5. Analytics data will start appearing in the dashboard after receiving visitor traffic

The implementation follows Vercel's best practices and is ready for deployment.
